    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **274 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners. The change satisfies the spec \u2014 each new owner gets `membershipNumber = current owner count + 1`, returned in the owner response as an integer field.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` (int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in API responses.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membershipNumber` column with getter/setter (mirroring the existing `registrationDate` field). MapStruct maps it to/from the DTO automatically by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, set `owner.setMembershipNumber(clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1)` right before saving (after the duplicate checks), so the value is one more than the current number of owners.\n\n4. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `membership_number INTEGER` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas.\n\nBecause the value is persisted, it's returned both from the create response and from `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which is what the `Cp09Tests` acceptance test reads back). The test confirms two consecutive creations differ by exactly one.",
